                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="aG2ArLrbdNIYtWfDBRse-2" parent="aG2ArLrbdNIYtWfDBRse-1" style="text;strokeColor=default;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;" value="&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;worker_threads&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; creates threads in the same process. They each get their own V8 isolate and event loop, but can share memory through &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;SharedArrayBuffer&lt;/code&gt; and pass messages cheaply." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="90" width="400" y="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="aG2ArLrbdNIYtWfDBRse-3" parent="aG2ArLrbdNIYtWfDBRse-1" style="text;strokeColor=default;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;" value="&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;child_process&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;spawn&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;exec&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;fork&lt;/code&gt;) starts a new OS process. Use &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;spawn&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;exec&lt;/code&gt; to run other programs (like &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;ffmpeg&lt;/code&gt; or a shell command), and &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;fork&lt;/code&gt; to start another Node.js process that talks to the parent over an IPC channel. The &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;cluster&lt;/code&gt; module is built on this: it forks several Node processes to use all cores for a server." vertex="1">
